TITLE:: SDGSampleTags
summary:: every sample of the library analysed and tagged: tags, bpm, key, dates, what was set by hand
categories:: Libraries>SuperDirtGUI
related:: Classes/SampleFeatures, Classes/SuperDirtGUI, Classes/SDGWindow, Classes/SampleEditor

DESCRIPTION::
What the sound explorer sorts and narrows by, and what Tidal picks samples by.
Every sample of the library is analysed once (link::Classes/SampleFeatures::,
of the sc-sample-editor quark, looked up by name: without it nothing is
analysed) and gets tags from the numbers; you add tags, take them away, set a bpm or a key,
and those are kept apart from the analysis, so analysing again never loses
them. Made by link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-tags::.

code::
t = ~sdg.tags;
t.analyseLibrary;                                // in the background
p = ~sdg.bufferAt(\bd, 0).path;
t.infoOf(p);                                     // (tags:, bpm:, bpmSure:, key:, keySure: ...)
t.addTag(p, "dusty"); t.removeTag(p, \kick);
t.setBpm(p, 92); t.setKey(p, "Am");
t.query([\percussive, \short], [\melodic]);      // [[\bd, 0], [\sn, 3] ...]
t.query(bpm: 120);                               // also 60, 240, 30, 480, within 3%
t.query(key: "am", bank: \superpiano);
t.allTags;                                       // tag -> how many samples
::

A sample is known by its path. Its analysis is redone when the file's size or
modification time changes. The tags the analysis gives:

table::
## code::short:: code::medium:: code::long:: || how long it sounds, to 20 dB under its peak: under 0.25 s, under 1.5 s, longer
## code::oneshot:: || one attack, under two seconds
## code::loop:: || a sure bpm, and the file a whole number of beats long
## code::percussive:: || a fast attack and a short decay; or three attacks a second with little pitch
## code::sustained:: || a level that holds for half a second or more
## code::melodic:: || a key, or the note of a one-shot
## code::noisy:: || a spectrum close to noise
## code::kick:: code::snare:: code::hat:: code::bass:: || guesses from the shape and where the energy is
## code::bright:: code::dark:: || the spectral centroid, over 3 kHz or under 250 Hz
## code::bpm-unsure:: code::key-unsure:: || a bpm or key the analysis does not trust
::

Good guesses, not truths: change what is wrong by hand. The long version, with
how each is measured, is code::docs/sample-tags.md::.

subsection:: Where it is kept

Two tab-separated files in link::#*folder::: code::analysis.tsv::, the numbers
(delete it to analyse everything again), and code::tags.tsv::, what was set by
hand (a code::.bak:: of the last version beside it). Nothing is ever written
into a bank's own folder. Writes wait a moment, so a queue of a hundred files
writes once; link::#-save:: writes now.

It sends code::changed:: with code::\tags:: (a path, or nil for many) and
code::\analysis:: (done, total) while the queue runs.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: features
code::SampleFeatures::, of the sc-sample-editor quark, or nil when it is not
installed: then nothing is analysed, and what was set by hand still works.

METHOD:: parseKey
code::"Am"::, code::"F#"::, code::"eb major"::, code::"C4":: as
code::(tonic: 0..11, mode: \major, \minor or \note)::, or nil. The same as
code::SampleFeatures.parseKey::, kept here so key searches work without it.
ARGUMENT:: str
the key.

METHOD:: noteNames
code::["C", "C#" ... "B"]::.

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: sdg
the link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI:: whose library it describes. Reads both files.

METHOD:: folder
Where the files are: a folder in the user support directory by default.
Checks set it to a scratch folder.

METHOD:: recordsPath
METHOD:: manualPath
The two files.

METHOD:: autoAnalyse
true: the window analyses the library when it opens, and the tag picker when it
finds nothing.

METHOD:: bpmTolerance
How close a bpm query has to be, as a share; 0.03.

METHOD:: bpmMultiples
What a bpm query counts too, as factors of it: code::[0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4]::.

METHOD:: chunk
How many files have their dates read in one call to the system.

METHOD:: autoTags
The tags the numbers say.
ARGUMENT:: r
a record, as link::#*recordFrom:: makes.
RETURNS:: an Array of Symbols.

METHOD:: recordFrom
What is kept of the features of a file.
ARGUMENT:: f
link::Classes/SampleFeatures#*analyse::'s answer.
ARGUMENT:: path
the file.
ARGUMENT:: dates
code::[created, dateAdded]::, or nil.

METHOD:: normaliseTag
ARGUMENT:: str
anything.
RETURNS:: lowercase letters, digits, code::-:: and code::_::, as a Symbol; nil for nothing.

METHOD:: bpmMatches
ARGUMENT:: bpm
a sample's.
ARGUMENT:: target
what is asked for.
ARGUMENT:: tolerance
nil for link::#*bpmTolerance::.
ARGUMENT:: multiples
nil for link::#*bpmMultiples::.
RETURNS:: true when the bpm is within the tolerance of the target or one of its multiples.

METHOD:: bpmDistance
ARGUMENT:: bpm
ARGUMENT:: target
RETURNS:: how far apart they are as a ratio, the nearest multiple counted; inf for nil.

METHOD:: keyMatches
ARGUMENT:: info
link::#-infoOf::'s answer.
ARGUMENT:: key
a String, or an Event from link::Classes/SDGSampleTags#*parseKey::.
RETURNS:: true for the same tonic and mode; a note matches every key on its tonic.

METHOD:: fileDates
ARGUMENT:: paths
files.
RETURNS:: code::[created, dateAdded]:: per path, seconds since 1970, nil where the
system does not say: the birth time and Spotlight's date added on macOS, the
birth time on Linux, the modification time on Windows.

METHOD:: parseDate
ARGUMENT:: str
code::"2025-08-25 03:27:00 +0000"::.
RETURNS:: seconds since 1970, or nil.

METHOD:: readRecords
METHOD:: writeRecords
METHOD:: readManual
METHOD:: writeManual
METHOD:: recordKeys
The two files, read and written.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: infoOf
Everything known about a file, what was set by hand over the analysis.
ARGUMENT:: path
the file.
ARGUMENT:: check
false: take the last analysis without asking the file whether it changed - for
a list of thousands drawn often.
RETURNS:: an Event: code::analysed::, code::duration::, code::numChannels::,
code::sampleRate::, code::onsets::, code::beatOffset::, code::bpm::,
code::bpmSure::, code::bpmByHand::, code::key::, code::keySure::,
code::keyByHand::, code::tonic::, code::mode::, code::tags:: (what counts),
code::auto::, code::added::, code::removed::, code::created::, code::dateAdded::.

METHOD:: tagsOf
ARGUMENT:: path
ARGUMENT:: check
RETURNS:: the tags that count: the analysis's, less those taken away, with those added.

METHOD:: autoTagsOf
ARGUMENT:: path
RETURNS:: the analysis's tags.

METHOD:: recordOf
ARGUMENT:: path
ARGUMENT:: check
RETURNS:: the analysis of a file, or nil when there is none or the file changed since.

METHOD:: isAnalysed
ARGUMENT:: path
RETURNS:: whether a fresh analysis is kept.

METHOD:: addTag
METHOD:: removeTag
A tag on or off for one file, by hand.
ARGUMENT:: path
ARGUMENT:: tag
a String or Symbol, see link::#*normaliseTag::.

METHOD:: setTags
A file's tags as given, whatever the analysis said.
ARGUMENT:: path
ARGUMENT:: tags
an Array.

METHOD:: resetTags
Back to what the analysis says: tags, bpm and key.
ARGUMENT:: path

METHOD:: setBpm
A bpm by hand, sure from then on; nil goes back to the analysis's.
ARGUMENT:: path
ARGUMENT:: bpm
ARGUMENT:: offset
where a beat falls, seconds, or nil to keep it.

METHOD:: setBeatOffset
ARGUMENT:: path
ARGUMENT:: seconds

METHOD:: setKey
A key by hand; nil goes back to the analysis's.
ARGUMENT:: path
ARGUMENT:: key
code::"Am"::, code::"F#"::, code::"Eb"::, code::"C3"::.

METHOD:: analyse
One file, now, in the calling thread; unchanged since its last analysis, it is
not read again.
ARGUMENT:: path
ARGUMENT:: force
true analyses it whatever.
ARGUMENT:: dates
code::[created, dateAdded]::, or nil to ask the system.
RETURNS:: its record, or nil.

METHOD:: analyseLibrary
Every sample of the library with no fresh analysis, in the background.

METHOD:: enqueue
ARGUMENT:: paths
files to analyse in the background.
ARGUMENT:: front
true: before the rest of the queue.

METHOD:: prioritise
A bank to the front of the queue, as the explorer does when it is opened.
ARGUMENT:: bank

METHOD:: isAnalysing
METHOD:: done
METHOD:: total
METHOD:: routine
The queue: running or not, how far it has got.

METHOD:: stop
Empty the queue and stop it. link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-free:: does.

METHOD:: libraryPaths
METHOD:: pathsOf
The files of the whole library, or of one bank.
ARGUMENT:: bank

METHOD:: matches
ARGUMENT:: path
ARGUMENT:: include
tags it must have.
ARGUMENT:: exclude
tags it must not.
ARGUMENT:: bpm
nil, or a bpm it must match, multiples counted.
ARGUMENT:: key
nil, or a key.
ARGUMENT:: check
as for link::#-infoOf::.

METHOD:: query
The samples of the library that match, in bank order. Kept until a tag or the
library changes, so a pattern asking on every event costs a lookup.
ARGUMENT:: include
ARGUMENT:: exclude
ARGUMENT:: bpm
ARGUMENT:: key
As for link::#-matches::.
ARGUMENT:: bank
nil for the whole library.
RETURNS:: code::[[bank, index] ...]::.

METHOD:: allTags
RETURNS:: an IdentityDictionary: tag -> how many samples of the library have it.

METHOD:: records
METHOD:: manual
METHOD:: stamp
What is held: path -> record, path -> what was set by hand, and a count bumped on every change.

METHOD:: load
METHOD:: save
METHOD:: saveRecords
METHOD:: saveManual
The two files, read again or written now.

METHOD:: sdg
METHOD:: dirt
The loader and its SuperDirt.
